From 3ee8da68d7c322c8bd6220f685261b7deb0ae9a9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 10:45:24 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [DOSKUTSU] patch 0314 -- composite world cache, stage 3a
 (variant B)

Stage 3a of the composite world cache. THIS STAGE IS A CORRECTNESS GATE AND
IS EXPECTED TO BE SLOWER WHEN ENABLED: it rebuilds the composite
unconditionally every frame, so it pays both the compositing cost and the
blit-out cost with no key and no possible hit. It exists to prove the
composite is pixel-correct before stage 3b introduces the tile-aligned key
that produces the saving. Do not bank an fps number from it.

Why this and not more per-frame tile work: Round N measured
mode_draw_scene at 21.05 ms, 64% of a 32.8 ms in-loop frame on the POD-83,
and the two tile layers lay down 1.01 screenfuls in ~15.9 ms = 4.9 MB/s
against a measured 17 MB/s memcpy floor. About 11.3 ms/frame is cost above
the copy floor. Patch 0097's cache aimed at this and failed on a
pixel-granular key that missed on every camera move; this composites at a
tile-aligned origin and applies the sub-tile remainder at read-out, so a hit
survives 15 of every 16 pixels of camera travel.

VARIANT B, operator call. The cache holds the BG and FG tile layers only,
colorkeyed; the backdrop stays on its existing path and shows through. The
opaque variant that composites the backdrop in projects a larger saving
(hit 6.6 ms vs 19.9, against B's 9.7 vs 18.0) but needs all ~7 return paths
in map_draw_backdrop() redirected to an off-screen surface -- the exact code
family that has produced a black-region defect three times (0183, 0143/0157,
wave-54's black valley). Taking that risk in the one stage that cannot show
a benefit is the wrong order; moving the backdrop in later is a contained
follow-up once a hit rate exists. Excluding it also removes the BK_PARALLAX
problem outright, since a world-origin key is wrong for a parallax backdrop
and the backdrop is no longer cached.

Declines rather than clamps on negative scroll: a clamp would silently shift
the world by a few pixels on the MAP_BORDER paths. Every declined case falls
through to map_draw(false), so the uncached path is byte-identical to
pre-0314.

The tile-selection logic mirrors _tilemap_render_plain_tiles_into_cache
exactly -- same special-case skips, same TA_CURRENT and 0x43 exclusions,
same PERF_MODE cut -- so the composite cannot disagree with the uncached
path about which tiles exist. Only the destination origin differs.

Counters are real counters, not literals. The plan's sec. 1.1 found
tm_route_cache hard-coded to 0, which misled every reader of those logs.
The 86 KB allocation is counted and logged rather than hand-waved.

Default-OFF behind strict SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_WORLD_CACHE=1.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/game.cpp |  10 ++-
 src/map.cpp  | 208 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/map.h    |   9 +++
 3 files changed, 226 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/game.cpp b/src/game.cpp
index decb41b1..a97cc126 100644
--- a/src/game.cpp
+++ b/src/game.cpp
@@ -1227,7 +1227,15 @@ void DrawScene(void)
       NXE::Diag::g_mds_decomp_pass = NXE::Diag::MDS_PASS_BG; // patch 0147
       {
         NXE::Diag::MdtBgTilelayerTimer _mtbg_tl;
-        map_draw(false);
+        // DOS-PORT (patch 0314, stage 3a): the world cache composites the BG
+        // AND FG tile layers into an off-screen tile-aligned surface and
+        // blits the sub-tile window out. It returns false whenever it
+        // declines, so the uncached call below stays byte-identical to
+        // pre-0314 behaviour. FG is still redrawn in full after the sprite
+        // pass -- narrowing that to a sprite-intersection repair set is
+        // stage 3c, not this one.
+        if (!world_cache_draw_tiles())
+          map_draw(false);
       }
     }
 
diff --git a/src/map.cpp b/src/map.cpp
index 89dbc566..21ddde86 100644
--- a/src/map.cpp
+++ b/src/map.cpp
@@ -3564,6 +3564,214 @@ void tilemap_cache_reset()
 // Original per-tile loop preserved in `_tilemap_render_uncached_full_-
 // loop()` (anonymous namespace above) for the killswitch / disabled
 // paths.
+// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+// DOS-PORT (patch 0314, Option 3 STAGE 3a): composite world cache.
+//
+// THIS STAGE IS A CORRECTNESS GATE AND IS EXPECTED TO BE SLOWER WHEN ENABLED.
+// It rebuilds the composite unconditionally every frame (no key, no hit), so
+// it pays the compositing cost AND the blit-out cost. It exists to prove the
+// composite is pixel-correct before stage 3b introduces the tile-aligned key
+// that actually produces the saving. Do not bank an fps number from it.
+//
+// VARIANT B (operator call): the cache holds the BG and FG TILE layers only.
+// The backdrop stays on its existing path and is drawn to the window first;
+// the cache is colorkeyed so the backdrop shows through wherever no tile is
+// laid down. Variant A -- an opaque cache with the backdrop composited in --
+// projects a larger saving (hit 6.6 ms vs 19.9, against B's 9.7 vs 18.0) but
+// requires redirecting all ~7 return paths inside map_draw_backdrop() to an
+// off-screen surface, and that is the exact code family that has produced a
+// black-region defect three separate times (0183, 0143/0157, wave-54's black
+// valley). Taking that risk in the one stage that by construction cannot show
+// a benefit is the wrong order. Moving the backdrop in later is a contained
+// follow-up once a hit rate is measured, not a rewrite.
+//
+// A second consequence of B, worth stating because the plan flagged it as an
+// open risk: excluding the backdrop removes the BK_PARALLAX problem entirely.
+// A world-origin key is wrong for a parallax backdrop, but the backdrop is no
+// longer in the cache, so parallax maps need no special-casing here.
+//
+// GEOMETRY. The surface is one tile wider and taller than the screen
+// (336x256 at 320x240) and is composited at a TILE-ALIGNED origin. The
+// sub-tile remainder is applied at read-out by offsetting the source rect, so
+// a hit survives 15 of every 16 pixels of camera travel -- the fix for patch
+// 0097's pixel-granular key, which missed on every camera move.
+//
+// The tile-selection logic below deliberately mirrors
+// _tilemap_render_plain_tiles_into_cache() (special-case skips, TA_CURRENT
+// and tilecode 0x43 exclusions, the PERF_MODE cut) so the composite cannot
+// disagree with the uncached path about WHICH tiles exist. The only
+// difference is the destination origin.
+// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+static SDL_Surface *g_world_cache_sfc = nullptr;
+static int      g_world_cache_w             = 0;
+static int      g_world_cache_h             = 0;
+static int      g_world_cache_decided       = -1;
+static unsigned g_world_cache_frames_block  = 0;
+static unsigned g_world_cache_composite_block = 0;
+static unsigned g_world_cache_declined_block  = 0;
+static unsigned g_world_cache_bytes         = 0;
+static bool     g_world_cache_first_logged  = false;
+
+static bool world_cache_enabled()
+{
+  if (g_world_cache_decided < 0)
+  {
+    const char *e = std::getenv("SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_WORLD_CACHE");
+    g_world_cache_decided = (e && e[0] == '1' && e[1] == 0) ? 1 : 0;
+    LOG_INFO("world-cache: {} -- stage 3a composite (patch 0314; "
+             "opt-in SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_WORLD_CACHE=1, default OFF). "
+             "Variant B: BG+FG tile layers only, colorkeyed, backdrop stays "
+             "on its own path. Unconditional-miss correctness gate -- when "
+             "enabled it is EXPECTED to be slower, the saving arrives in 3b.",
+             g_world_cache_decided ? "ENABLED (opt-in)" : "DISABLED (default)");
+  }
+  return g_world_cache_decided == 1;
+}
+
+// Composite one tile layer into the cache at a tile-aligned origin.
+static void _world_cache_render_layer(SDL_Surface *cache, uint8_t foreground)
+{
+  if (!cache) return;
+  Renderer *r = Renderer::getInstance();
+  const bool drawtile_fast_bg_on = NXE::Diag::drawtile_fast_bg_active();
+  const int scroll_x = (map.displayed_xscroll / CSFI);
+  const int scroll_y = (map.displayed_yscroll / CSFI);
+  const int mapx = scroll_x / TILE_W;
+  const int mapy = scroll_y / TILE_H;
+
+  for (int y = 0; y <= (r->screenHeight / TILE_H) + MAP_DRAW_EXTRA_Y; y++)
+  {
+    for (int x = 0; x <= (r->screenWidth / TILE_W) + MAP_DRAW_EXTRA_X; x++)
+    {
+      if (((mapx + x) >= 0) && ((mapy + y) >= 0)
+          && ((mapx + x) < map.xsize) && ((mapy + y) < map.ysize))
+      {
+        const int t = map.tiles[mapx + x][mapy + y];
+        if (((game.curmap == 71) && (tilecode[t] == 0x41)) || ((game.curmap == 31)))
+        {
+        }
+        else if ((tileattr[t] & TA_FOREGROUND) == foreground
+                 && !_perf_b2_skip_fg_tile(tileattr[t], foreground))
+        {
+          if (!(tileattr[t] & TA_CURRENT) && tilecode[t] != 0x43)
+          {
+            // Tile-aligned destination: no sub-tile offset here, it is
+            // applied at read-out instead.
+            ++NXE::Diag::g_drawtile_fast_bg_calls_count_block;
+            if (drawtile_fast_bg_on)
+            {
+              ++NXE::Diag::g_drawtile_fast_bg_engaged_count_block;
+              r->tileset.drawTileFastToSurface(cache, x * TILE_W, y * TILE_H, t);
+            }
+            else
+            {
+              ++NXE::Diag::g_drawtile_fast_bg_fallback_count_block;
+              r->tileset.drawTileToSurface(cache, x * TILE_W, y * TILE_H, t);
+            }
+          }
+        }
+      }
+    }
+  }
+}
+
+// Returns true when the cache handled the BG tile layer, in which case the
+// caller must NOT run map_draw(false). Returns false for every declined case
+// so the uncached path stays byte-identical to pre-0314 behaviour.
+bool world_cache_draw_tiles()
+{
+  if (!world_cache_enabled()) return false;
+  if (flipacceltime) return false;
+
+  Renderer *r = Renderer::getInstance();
+  if (!r) return false;
+  SDL_Surface *win = r->_cached_window_surface;
+  if (!win) return false;
+
+  ++g_world_cache_frames_block;
+
+  const int scroll_x = (map.displayed_xscroll / CSFI);
+  const int scroll_y = (map.displayed_yscroll / CSFI);
+  // Negative scroll would make the read-out source rect negative, which is
+  // not a valid blit. It happens on the MAP_BORDER paths. Decline rather
+  // than clamp -- a clamp would silently shift the world by a few pixels.
+  if (scroll_x < 0 || scroll_y < 0)
+  {
+    ++g_world_cache_declined_block;
+    return false;
+  }
+
+  const int cw = r->screenWidth + TILE_W;
+  const int ch = r->screenHeight + TILE_H;
+
+  if (g_world_cache_sfc && (g_world_cache_w != cw || g_world_cache_h != ch))
+  {
+    SDL_DestroySurface(g_world_cache_sfc);
+    g_world_cache_sfc = nullptr;
+  }
+  if (!g_world_cache_sfc)
+  {
+    g_world_cache_sfc = SDL_CreateSurface(cw, ch, win->format);
+    if (!g_world_cache_sfc)
+    {
+      ++g_world_cache_declined_block;
+      return false;
+    }
+    if (win->format == SDL_PIXELFORMAT_INDEX8 && r->masterPalette())
+      SDL_SetSurfacePalette(g_world_cache_sfc, r->masterPalette());
+    SDL_SetSurfaceColorKey(g_world_cache_sfc, true, TILEMAP_FG_COLORKEY);
+    g_world_cache_w = cw;
+    g_world_cache_h = ch;
+    // Count the allocation rather than hand-waving it: the RAM floor is a
+    // measured 16 MB and this rides on top of the existing caches.
+    g_world_cache_bytes = (unsigned)(g_world_cache_sfc->pitch * ch);
+    LOG_INFO("world-cache: allocated {}x{} INDEX8 colorkeyed, pitch={} "
+             "bytes={} (screen {}x{} + one tile margin)",
+             cw, ch, g_world_cache_sfc->pitch, g_world_cache_bytes,
+             r->screenWidth, r->screenHeight);
+  }
+
+  // STAGE 3a: unconditional miss. Rebuild every frame. No key is consulted
+  // and no hit is possible -- that is 3b's job. The counter below is a REAL
+  // counter, not a literal: sec. 1.1 of the plan found `tm_route_cache` was
+  // hard-coded to 0 and it misled every reader of those logs, including this
+  // author. Do not reintroduce that pattern.
+  ++g_world_cache_composite_block;
+  SDL_FillSurfaceRect(g_world_cache_sfc, NULL, TILEMAP_FG_COLORKEY);
+  _world_cache_render_layer(g_world_cache_sfc, 0);
+  _world_cache_render_layer(g_world_cache_sfc, 1);
+
+  SDL_Rect src;
+  src.x = scroll_x % TILE_W;
+  src.y = scroll_y % TILE_H;
+  src.w = r->screenWidth;
+  src.h = r->screenHeight;
+  SDL_Rect dst;
+  dst.x = 0;
+  dst.y = 0;
+  dst.w = r->screenWidth;
+  dst.h = r->screenHeight;
+  SDL_BlitSurface(g_world_cache_sfc, &src, win, &dst);
+
+  if (!g_world_cache_first_logged)
+  {
+    g_world_cache_first_logged = true;
+    LOG_INFO("world-cache: first composite (src={},{} {}x{} curmap={} "
+             "scrolltype={}) -- stage 3a unconditional miss",
+             src.x, src.y, src.w, src.h, game.curmap, map.scrolltype);
+  }
+  if ((g_world_cache_frames_block % 100) == 0)
+  {
+    LOG_INFO("[world-cache n={} composites={} declined={} bytes={}]",
+             g_world_cache_frames_block, g_world_cache_composite_block,
+             g_world_cache_declined_block, g_world_cache_bytes);
+    g_world_cache_frames_block    = 0;
+    g_world_cache_composite_block = 0;
+    g_world_cache_declined_block  = 0;
+  }
+  return true;
+}
+
 void map_draw(uint8_t foreground)
 {
   Renderer *r = Renderer::getInstance();
diff --git a/src/map.h b/src/map.h
index afefaf28..35482032 100644
--- a/src/map.h
+++ b/src/map.h
@@ -139,6 +139,15 @@ void DrawFastLeftLayered(void);
 // map_draw_backdrop runs). Scoped to DrawScene caller, not the
 // backdrop function's internals.
 bool map_backdrop_should_skip_clear_and_draw();
+
+// DOS-PORT (patch 0314, stage 3a): composite world cache, variant B (BG+FG
+// tile layers only; the backdrop stays on its own path and shows through the
+// colorkey). Returns true when it has drawn the tile layers, in which case
+// the caller must NOT also run map_draw(false). Returns false for every
+// declined case, leaving the uncached path byte-identical to pre-0314.
+// Unconditional-miss correctness gate -- EXPECTED to be slower when enabled.
+// Opt-in via SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_WORLD_CACHE=1, default OFF.
+bool world_cache_draw_tiles();
 void map_backdrop_record_present_success();
 void map_backdrop_invalidate_skip_state();
 
